          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can you seal stamped concrete yourself as a DIY project?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Yes, sealing stamped concrete is a manageable DIY project for most homeowners with basic tool skills. The critical success factors are thorough surface cleaning, complete drying before application, and applying thin even coats rather than one thick coat. The most common DIY mistake is over-application, which causes bubbling, whitening, and peeling. Use a three-eighths-inch nap roller, apply two thin coats with four to six hours between them, and you will achieve professional-looking results. Budget approximately three to four hours for a typical 300-square-foot patio.
            </p>
