          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Why is my stamped concrete sealer turning white?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              White discoloration in stamped concrete sealer is almost always caused by moisture trapped beneath the sealer film. This happens when sealer is applied to damp concrete, when rain falls before the sealer fully cures, or when ground moisture migrates upward through the slab. For light whitening, applying a thin coat of xylene will re-dissolve the acrylic film and allow trapped moisture to escape as it re-cures. For severe whitening, the affected sealer must be fully stripped and reapplied under proper dry conditions. Prevention is always easier than cure — ensure the concrete is completely dry and check the weather forecast before sealing.
            </p>
